AOT code caches for WoW64: block linking only through data

Port of patches/fex/0003 (FEX 14c9268) to Madeira's FEX (3bec2ac), on top
of 0007. With AOTCodeCacheWIP, jump thunks no longer carry their
ExitFunctionLinkData record. The record lives in the AOT data area (three
slots, numbered with the data slots of 0007) and the thunk reaches it with
adrp + add (RELOC_GUEST_RIP_LINK_RECORD):

    adrp TMP1, Record; add TMP1, TMP1, :lo12:Record
    ldr TMP2, [TMP1]; cbz TMP2, 1f; br TMP2
 1: mov lr, TMP1; ldr TMP2, [STATE, ExitFunctionLinker]; br TMP2

The loader fills each record with HostCode 0, the guest RIP and CallerOffset
DATA_ONLY_LINK_RECORD. For such records ExitFunctionLink only stores HostCode
and the delinker only clears it, so neither the call site nor the thunk is
ever patched. On iOS the data area sits next to the code in the dual-mapped
JIT pool, so both stores go through the RW alias (DualMap::WriteAddr).

